{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "Q9UGM1", "secondaryAccessions": ["Q14CY7", "Q4W5A2", "Q9NYV2"], "uniProtkbId": "ACHA9_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "2001-04-27", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-06-10", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2010-10-05", "entryVersion": 199, "sequenceVersion": 2}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Neuronal acetylcholine receptor subunit alpha-9"}}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "Nicotinic acetylcholine receptor subunit alpha-9"}, "shortNames": [{"value": "NACHR alpha-9"}]}], "flag": "Precursor"}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000312", "source": "HGNC", "id": "HGNC:14079"}], "value": "CHRNA9"}, "synonyms": [{"value": "NACHRA9"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P43144"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11021840"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11752216"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18723036"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "25282151"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18723036"}], "value": "Component of neuronal acetylcholine receptors (nAChRs) that function as pentameric, ligand-gated cation channels with high calcium permeability among other activities. nAChRs are excitatory neurotrasnmitter receptors formed by a collection of nAChR subunits known to mediate synaptic transmission in the nervous system and the neuromuscular junction. Each nAchR subunit confers differential attributes to channel properties, including activation, deactivation and desensitization kinetics, pH sensitivity, cation permeability, and binding to allosteric modulators (PubMed:11752216, PubMed:18723036, PubMed:25282151). Forms either homopentamers or heteropentamers with CHRNA10. Expressed in the inner ear, in sympathetic neurons and in other non-neuronal cells, such as skin keratinocytes and lymphocytes (PubMed:11752216, PubMed:18723036). nAChR formed by CHRNA9:CHRNA10 mediate central nervous system control of auditory and vestibular sensory processing. The channel is permeable to a range of divalent cations including calcium, the influx of which may activate a potassium current which hyperpolarizes the cell membrane (PubMed:11752216, PubMed:25282151). In the ear, mediates synaptic transmission between efferent olivocochlear fibers and hair cells of the cochlea, this may lead to a reduction in basilar membrane motion, altering the activity of auditory nerve fibers and reducing the range of dynamic hearing. This may protect against acoustic trauma (By similarity). May also regulate keratinocyte adhesion (PubMed:11021840, PubMed:11752216, PubMed:25282151)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "Ca(2+)(in) = Ca(2+)(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:29671"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29108"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11752216"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "K(+)(in) = K(+)(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:29463"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29103"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P43144"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "Na(+)(in) = Na(+)(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:34963"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29101"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P43144"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "Mg(2+)(in) = Mg(2+)(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:29827"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:18420"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P43144"}]}}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "22774872"}], "value": "Activated by a myriad of ligands such as acetylcholine (PubMed:22774872). AChR activity is inhibited by the antagonist alpha-conotoxins RgIA and GeXXA, small disulfide-constrained peptides from cone snails (PubMed:22774872)"}], "commentType": "ACTIVITY REGULATION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P43144"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11752216"}], "value": "Forms homo- or heteropentameric channels in conjunction with CHRNA10 (PubMed:11752216). The native outer hair cell receptor is composed of CHRNA9:CHRNA10 heterooligomers. Found in the stoichiometric form (CHRNA9)2:(CHRNA10)3 (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "INTERACTION", "interactions": [{"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q9UGM1", "intActId": "EBI-9008641"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P60616", "intActId": "EBI-16123259"}, "numberOfExperiments": 2, "organismDiffer": true}]}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Synaptic cell membrane", "id": "SL-0531"}, "topology": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}], "value": "Multi-pass membrane protein", "id": "SL-9909"}}, {"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "25282151"}], "value": "Cell membrane", "id": "SL-0039"}, "topology": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}], "value": "Multi-pass membrane protein", "id": "SL-9909"}}]}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11021840"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11752216"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "15531379"}], "value": "Expressed in cochlea, keratinocytes, pituitary gland, B-cells and T-cells"}], "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "25282151"}], "value": "N-glycosylated"}], "commentType": "PTM"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11752216"}], "value": "The heterooligomeric receptor composed of CHRNA9 and CHRNA10 has an atypical pharmacological profile, binding several non-nicotinic ligands including strychnine (a glycine receptor antagonist) and atropine (a muscarinic acetylcholine receptor antagonist)"}], "commentType": "MISCELLANEOUS"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Belongs to the ligand-gated ion channel (TC 1.A.9) family. Acetylcholine receptor (TC 1.A.9.1) subfamily. Alpha-9/CHRNA9 sub-subfamily"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}], "features": [{"type": "Signal", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 22, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}]}, {"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 23, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 479, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Neuronal acetylcholine receptor subunit alpha-9", "featureId": "PRO_0000000371"}, {"type": "Topological domain", "location": {"start": {"value": 23, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 238, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Extracellular", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}]}, {"type": "Transmembrane", "location": {"start": {"value": 239, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 259, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Helical", "evidences": [